http://code.google.com/p/csa-c/

which isn't Akima's method but might also be useful.

I can see three steps:

    Establish a baseline for packages depending on, importing, or suggesting akima directly or indirectly;
    Establish what C/C++ code is available with compatible licences;
    Interface the available code to R and check the benchmarks, if not OK, see what needs to be implemented, continue until the benchmarks pass.

Hope this clarifies,

Roger

