MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear All,

I am Khurram and I am a PhD student in Computer Vision at UCF. I am interested in working for R-project and would like to contribute to the open source community. In todays world where everyone owns a camera, there is a huge amount of data in the form of images and videos that people try to analyze and perform useful things like: actions recognition, object detection, tracking, etc. After having a detailed look at the current packages related to Computer Vision in the R repository, I felt the need for a good package, that would cover major algorithms in this area and would be something to build upon for later programmers to come. I compiled the following list of algorithms/functions that are being used frequently in MATLAB/OpenCV/etc and would be something really useful for users of R-project:-

1.Edge Detection: Canny, Sobel, Prewitt, Marr Hildreth

2.Feature Extraction: Harris Corner Detector, HOG (Histogram of Oriented Gradients)

3.Optical Flow: Horn & Shunk, Lucas-Kanade with Pyramids

4.Global Motion (Bergan et. al, Mann Picard) and Video Mosaicing

5.Background Modeling and Object Detection using Mixture of Gaussians

6.Hough Transform: Line Fitting, Circle Fitting, Generalized Hough Transform

7.Segmentation: using Clustering,Histogram, Region Growing.

8.Image Operations:

                                    - RGB to Gray Scale

                                    - Convolution

                                    - Correlation

                                    - Derivatives

                                    - Mask generation for above operations: (Gaussian, Average, derivative,etc)

                                    - Morphological Operations: dilate, erode, etc

                                    - Image Histogram

                                    - Connected Components

9. Image Spatial Transformations: Translation, Rotation, Shear, Scale and Affine.

10.RANSAC(RANdom SAmple Consensus) for line fitting and Homography

11.Color Space Transformations: RGB to LUV, RGB to LAB, RGB to HSV, etc

This could be a good starting point to provide useful tools which can be further enhanced in near future.

If this idea is appreciated I would like to provide references to their publication/source for the above list of algorithms.

I am looking forward to know your opinions about the current list of functionality and any additions that you would like to suggest.

--
Thanks,
Khurram Soomro

